[{"id":"VRCE-3-12-1","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":12,"verse":1,"english":"'O Rāma, I am pleased with you; good betide you! And, O Laksmana, I am gratified by you. You are in trouble in consequence of the great fatigue that you have undergone on the way. And Janaka's daughter, the noble Maithili, is evidently cager (for rest).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3012001","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f74efab77c11c6c3c795e454329684f336041c543c911b724c48aa43238d7f5a","compact":"205434c662a68b81a39f27f24000dc4910c978b264a41039fcd1f7d1059a67e6","nasal":"205434c662a68b81a39f27f24000dc4910c978b264a41039fcd1f7d1059a67e6"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-12-2","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":12,"verse":2,"english":"'O Rāma, I am pleased with you; good betide you! And, O Laksmana, I am gratified by you. You are in trouble in consequence of the great fatigue that you have undergone on the way. And Janaka's daughter, the noble Maithili, is evidently cager (for rest).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3012002","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"20f472663c4b0ae7309c6ac2e3a043b5b3e40a527df47c41848efd8b6d67c8ef","compact":"38e1ec05ef57a0b1df333b17e11816b6022e7b00ac6a2d217223a3902b8f240b","nasal":"c03f718f2825487d96163b9c8c7ec704db4589a7ca828c0447935ab461ca5345"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-12-3","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":12,"verse":3,"english":"Of tender years and unkn wn to hardship, she has come to the forest rife with troubles, being urged by the love she bears to her lord.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.641,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3012003","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e5767b731ac51082c8510281667d5feeb2d98acd47182df1c4d36907141be4ab","compact":"062d11d6137ab50c549da64600857c358c2ef49e5e25b7eaff85c155b10e3444","nasal":"062d11d6137ab50c549da64600857c358c2ef49e5e25b7eaff85c155b10e3444"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-12-4","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":12,"verse":4,"english":"Do you, O Rāma, conduct yourself so, that Sītā may find a pleasant time of it. By fcllowing you to the forest, it is a hard task that she is performing.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.843,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3012004","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6c858784d210d8475606a7dda7e0b850ff300b792f65b021adb71277a7709787","compact":"29f7d0ce47f57f7f3310cce180eb1df9f73b941eb3380b8ee80ba1923600ab16","nasal":"29f7d0ce47f57f7f3310cce180eb1df9f73b941eb3380b8ee80ba1923600ab16"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-12-5","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":12,"verse":5,"english":"O son of Raghu, this has been the nature of the fair sex from the commencement of creation, that they gladden him that is well off, and forsake a person in adversity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.905,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3012005","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"440e45240b11ebcffdbb8c5cde0f839cee650d76134e7495a830dd041209f3d5","compact":"175013706953f7106dcc9bca0e8d95142d1f37f37b8121f6775efd94be78c2a7","nasal":"53460a58fd96fa567b1a4f07cdd94155bbfa38e6b8ab3365775da72482a7aec2"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-12-6","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":12,"verse":6,"english":"And women imitate the instability of lightning, the sharpness of weapons, and the celerity of Garuda and the wind.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.809,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3012006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"936372d7a7922d4b5c5ecf350144064972fb5d9ea1ee6e84460ad89438fbae29","compact":"951cf291f7addba0aed24b830fe972a16268c31c647af8648d19a2832913c4f2","nasal":"9b5bda72105b86238feaf8c879e98ed8cbab639df7ef6baeb442a10d84cb55a7"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-12-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":12,"verse":7,"english":"But this wife of yours is absolutely free from all these defects; she is worthy of being extolled and the foremost of those devoted to their lord, like Arundhati among the gods.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.708,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3012007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9f65d6e849cb20eaa385059b8b66d0a494b5b7fc6bebb549f31b14820e49be1d","compact":"049dd81021d19a8c55e0e93e0a170e4f4c773798aedbe3999deefd52d56e3505","nasal":"1222c85eefafaba36df9a249e44d7f140a1a0e7b53bc5f1a086d4c2dbd9de62d"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-12-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":12,"verse":8,"english":"This region, O Rāma, will be adorned, since, O subduer of enemies, you along with Vaidehī and Sumitra's son, will dwell here.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3012008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ff337a41cb9a853fbec2600ae640ab923c836c6ba5b789e098ba5dd4dd8d3742","compact":"1a913b61dd71f87efc53eed65f2dad748e1ec54e4d141063aabe114b8160c7c8","nasal":"1a913b61dd71f87efc53eed65f2dad748e1ec54e4d141063aabe114b8160c7c8"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-12-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":12,"verse":9,"english":"Thus addressed by the ascetic, Rāghava, joining his hands, humbly observed to that saint resembling flaming fire,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3012009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e26c2f5fc625ba35a76f6504a330688c34f836d80a149de4844bed2061be96b3","compact":"2df14ad133e9200ee499c7796fa853e7ab6015eaf41b184c1ab150b835ab947f","nasal":"5ae663f67432f9eda8643dd4479568e5398e4990f44fc6a4cdf1b713eebbf0c2"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-12-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":12,"verse":10,"english":"Blessed and beholden am I, since the foremost of ascetics is gratified with my merits as well as with those of my brother and wife.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.846,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3012010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"91868a308293c5256768134c541addefed819526fccafe7342255f1abdd8ce46","compact":"be4af1e1c846fa328b627c462b5638fbbb741bce71ed5aa2b6b0336ab7804182","nasal":"be4af1e1c846fa328b627c462b5638fbbb741bce71ed5aa2b6b0336ab7804182"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-12-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":12,"verse":11,"english":"Do you now direct me to a country well watered, and abounding in woods, where rearing an asylum, 1 may dwell delightfully and pleasantly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3012011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"644f9fd17f9441a20ca8db1480001cd7fac36a9d0854bec1adbb721a51276090","compact":"767964bdad1547e8f621a14348edd56b0f94b9164909decaebfd7be72fc14a17","nasal":"767964bdad1547e8f621a14348edd56b0f94b9164909decaebfd7be72fc14a17"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-12-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":12,"verse":12,"english":"Hearing Rāma's words, that best of ascetics, reflecting for a while, spoke these excellent words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.716,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3012012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bd16ab193f4c4e53002e9193c9da911ba96bee62495e701abb376a76beb2e892","compact":"b604e8485b40a108d04cf30021751fc311103872af8de0b88341739606ecb92f","nasal":"b604e8485b40a108d04cf30021751fc311103872af8de0b88341739606ecb92f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-12-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":12,"verse":13,"english":"Two Yojanas hence, my child, is a region abounding in fruits and roots, containing countless deer, and beautiful-known by the name of Pancavați.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3012013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ec54939132a8d58f4a2fd51a40534a07a5b47b61403142c5ad0133eff3c249bb","compact":"64676e4fd1fe6a5ae9a92a833b76e05b4cb8b132d2dc0d071fb02821d9a029dd","nasal":"dba0fe89c2e7fbe46884a305ab5a77654dae3c94947548e3eb68000eb4385a06"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-12-14","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":12,"verse":14,"english":"Repairing thither, do you, rearing an asylum, pass your time pleasantly in company with Sumitrā's son, duly doing the mandate of your sire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-12-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3012014","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8a7ea93efafd8bfa488159a0eab450856830775194185f9129f3e784dc2d33c3","compact":"a1426908bf39b0c96ef